  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New table `crates/ui/src/cli_options.rs`. It lists each start option and each environment variable. The option check and the `--help` text read this one table.\n- `--help`, `-h` and `--version` print and exit with code 0. This happens before any window or GPU device is made.\n- An unknown option exits with code 2. The message names the option and points to `--help`.\n- New user guide page `docs/user-guide/start-options.md`.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2082-help-options.md`.\n\n## Printed `--help` text\n\n```\ncamcraft-ui - a CAM program that turns 3D models into NC programs\n\nUsage: camcraft-ui [options]\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help\n      Print this text and exit. No window opens.\n      Default: off\n  --version\n      Print the program version and exit. No window opens.\n      Default: off\n  --headless\n      Start with no window. Run a short self-check of the 3D view and exit.\n      Default: off\n  --ui <name>\n      Choose the user interface. Only \"egui\" exists.\n      Default: egui\n  --gpu-backend <dx12|metal|vulkan|gl>\n      Try this graphics system first. The other systems stay as a fallback.\n      Environment variable: CAMCRAFT_GPU_BACKEND. The option wins over the variable.\n      Default: automatic\n  --gpu <adapter name>\n      Use the graphics card whose name holds this text. Capitals do not matter.\n      Environment variable: CAMCRAFT_GPU. The option wins over the variable.\n      Default: automatic\n  --mcp-port <port>\n      Open the MCP server for AI agents on this local port (0 to 65535).\n      Environment variable: CAMCRAFT_MCP_PORT. The option wins over the variable.\n      Default: off\n\nEnvironment variables:\n  CAMCRAFT_GPU_BACKEND <dx12|metal|vulkan|gl>\n      Same as --gpu-backend.\n  CAMCRAFT_GPU <adapter name>\n      Same as --gpu.\n  CAMCRAFT_MCP_PORT <port>\n      Same as --mcp-port.\n  CAMCRAFT_LOG <filter>\n      How much the log says, for example debug. RUST_LOG is the fallback.\n      Default: info, with quiet graphics libraries\n  CAMCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR <folder>\n      Folder for the list of recent files.\n      Default: the user settings folder of the system\n  CAMCRAFT_MACHINES <folder>\n      Folder for the user machine files.\n      Default: camcraft/machines in the user data folder\n  CAMCRAFT_FIXTURES <folder>\n      Folder for the user fixture library.\n      Default: the user data folder\n  CAMCRAFT_THEMES <folder>\n      Folder that holds the theme files.\n      Default: assets/themes next to the program\n\nA value can follow as --option value or as --option=value.\n\n```\n\nUnknown option: `unknown option '--bogus'. Run camcraft-ui --help to see the options.` Exit code 2.\n\n## Tests (`camcraft-ui` lib, `cli_options_tests`)\n\n- `help_names_each_option_and_variable_of_the_table`\n- `each_flag_the_readers_use_is_in_the_table`\n- `each_table_option_is_accepted_by_the_parser`\n- `help_and_version_are_found_in_any_place`\n- `unknown_option_gives_an_error_that_names_it`\n- `run_refuses_unknown_option_with_code_2_and_opens_no_window`\n\nClippy on `camcraft-ui` with `-D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The old flag readers (`gpu.rs`, `mcp::port_from`) still have their own flag strings. A test pins that each is in the table. A new flag in a reader without a table row is not detected.\n- No full suite, no snapshot lane. No window was opened.\n- Not run on Linux or macOS.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-ui --help` now lists each start option and environment variable; `--version` added; an unknown option is refused with exit code 2.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2082\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
